# Proposed by the executor of F68 (2026-10-15), from what two adversarial readers played; the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: the next dock takes all that is left over, however much that is. But too little to show any window in is nothing: then everybody in
# the row gives, as with nothing left, and the window that was just docked, with the keyboard in it, is not typed into unseen.
# Reference: F68, F61.
quiet
# Xcode will not go under 1200 points, which leaves 204 of 1416. Terminal gets a half, and Xcode is the tile.
open Xcode 1300x800 min 1200x600
open Terminal 584x366 min 177x100
dock 101 left
focus 102
press dock right
expect visible 102
expect size 102 702x851
expect at 102 726 37
expect tile 101
expect focused 102
# Xcode closes: Terminal stays as it is. (It is not paid on top what the Desktop had lent to Xcode.)
close 101
expect still 102
expect size 102 702x851
close 102

# A gap dragged by hand until a sliver is left over. Safari has 700 points to spare.
open Safari 900x600 min 574x240
open Terminal 584x366 min 177x100
dock 103 left
seam 0 600
focus 104
dock 104 right
expect visible 103
expect visible 104
expect size 103 702x851
expect size 104 702x851
close 103
close 104

# The same with `makeRoom` off: it is no making of room.
set makeRoom false
open Safari 500x400
open Notes 500x400
dock 105 left
seam 0 500
focus 106
dock 106 right
expect visible 106
expect size 106 702x851
set makeRoom true
close 105
close 106

# Squeezed by hand against a neighbour until it is a tile, and the neighbour closes: with everything else left over nobody squeezes it.
open Safari 900x600 min 574x240
open Terminal 584x366 min 177x100
dock 107 left
dock 108 right
seam 0 -200
expect tile 107
focus 108
close 108
expect visible 107
expect size 107 574x851
